{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/119331","id":3648115405,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc7ZcdLN","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/119331","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/119331.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/119331.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/119331","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/119331/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/119331/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/119331/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/800223a04314319cbf569f359c5131d2595f0e29","number":119331,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"Release X11 pressed events on true focus loss","user":{"login":"norepro","id":30921834,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwOTIxODM0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/30921834?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/norepro","html_url":"https://github.com/norepro","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/norepro/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/norepro/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/norepro/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/norepro/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/norepro/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/norepro/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/norepro/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/norepro/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/norepro/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"There are two \"focus lost\" signals in the Godot X11 display server:\r\n\r\n1. `FocusOut` - native X11 signal\r\n\r\n2. `NOTIFICATION_APPLICATION_FOCUS_OUT` - Godot signal after 250ms of no other window getting focus.\r\n\r\nWhen focus is lost, the intent is to clear any input pressed events so that, when focus returns, we have a clean slate.\r\n\r\nThe bug is that the pressed events are (attempted to be) cleared on the first signal, X11's `FocusOut`. This is always a no-op because it returns early if the application still has focus. Godot's X11 server only sets that flag after the second signal, not the first.\r\n\r\nMove the pressed event clearing from the first signal handler to the second. This makes clearing pressed events do what it says.\r\n\r\nThis does not affect Wayland because it does not have the 250ms grace period.\r\n\r\nSimple repro is to load any 3D scene, hold 'W' and, while 'W' is held, click on any non-Godot window. Release 'W', click back to Godot, and hold RMB. It will zoom forward as if 'W' is still pressed.\r\n\r\nAfter the fix, the same test has RMB look around as expected when no other keys are pressed.\r\n\r\nFixes #118897\r\n\r\n<!--\r\nPlease target the `master` branch. We will take care of backporting relevant fixes to older versions.\r\n\r\nBefore submitting, please read our checklist for new contributors:\r\nhttps://contributing.godotengine.org/en/latest/engine/introduction.html#checklist-for-new-contributors\r\n-->\r\n","labels":[{"id":73330064,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2NA==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/bug","name":"bug","description":"","color":"ff6055","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279097326,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTczMjY=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/platform:linuxbsd","name":"platform:linuxbsd","description":"","color":"e4e4e4","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279098255,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTgyNTU=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:platforms","name":"top